## Goal
Make the decision graph tell a link settled by the "unmatched" panel apart from a user rule that happens to be named `none`. Also tidy the wording in ADR 0007 (DEV-50).

## Problems
None.

## Decision
`ResolvePaths` in `internal/serve/graph.go` now checks a new helper, `unmatchedAsked`. It is true when the rule column is `none` and the ask note starts with "asked (no rule)". Only the unmatched panel writes that note, so it identifies these decisions reliably. Such decisions get the path node `s:none`. All other decisions resolve through `logRuleID` as before, so a real rule named `none` keeps its `r:none` node. Matching on the note avoids changing the log format or reserving the name `none` for users.

A new test, `TestResolvePathsUnmatchedVersusRuleNamedNone` in `internal/serve/groups_test.go`, parses a rules file containing a rule named `none`. It checks three cases: an unmatched asked link, a plain match of the user's `none` rule, and an ordinary "asked -> Safari" link that went through that rule.

In `docs/adr/0007-remember-failure-notification.md`, the wording now says the handler log (stderr) reports a denied or undetermined notification permission.

